        "original_id": "e29997e4-7049-53fa-afba-245c3a2916f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Northwest Territories, Canada, Yellowknife\n- Projects: Tundra Mine, Negus Mine, Salmita Mine\n- Topics: gold mining, production, mining infrastructure\n\nFacts:\n- Negus Mine was a gold producer at Yellowknife in the Northwest Territories, Canada, from 1939 to 1952.\n- Tundra Mine was a gold producer in the Northwest Territories, Canada, from 1964 to 1968.\n- Tundra Mine produced 104,476 troy ounces (3,250 kg) of gold from 187,714 tons of ore.\n- Salmita Mine used the old camp and milling plant of the abandoned Tundra Mine, which was located a few kilometres to the south.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
